# App platform — core

For a **public web app in one AWS account** (this repo’s template pattern):

- **Hosting**: AWS **one account**, two environments (`stg` / `prod`). Terraform is the source of truth. Do **not** reintroduce CDK or manage app resources with CloudFormation.
- **GitHub env separation**: feature work → **`staging`** (AWS stg only). Promote via **`staging` → `main`** (AWS prod). GitHub Environments `staging` / `production` must use **distinct** roles, buckets, and distributions.
- **DNS**: Cloudflare app Terraform root is **DNS only**. Zone rulesets live in [`7oas7er/platform`](https://github.com/7oas7er/platform) `shared-edge` — never recreate them in an app root.
- **Observability**: Grafana Cloud Free only — see `app-observability`. Shared Infinity DS + GitHub **plugin** live in platform `shared-obs`; app grafana roots own dashboards/synthetics/CloudWatch/per-app GitHub DS only.
- **Cloudflare-only traffic**: accept only traffic that came through Cloudflare; reject direct origin (CloudFront URL, ALB DNS, etc.). Mechanism may vary; principle matters.
- **Secrets**: never commit `.tfstate`, `terraform.tfvars`, API tokens, or AWS keys. Local AWS profile `7oas7er`; GitHub Actions uses OIDC. See `SECURITY.md` for leak response.
- **Prefer small diffs**; match existing patterns.
- **Agents**: `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `docs/adr/`, `SECURITY.md`. New irreversible choice → short ADR under `docs/adr/`.
